london_crime.crime_by_lsoa – relevant columns and typical usage  

• `minor_category`: grouping key – we need the five most‑frequent categories in 2008 and again when calculating yearly shares.  
• `value`: the numeric measure to be aggregated (SUM).  
• `year`: filter for 2008 when finding the “top‑5”, and later to compute results for every year.  
(Other columns such as `lsoa_code`, `borough`, `major_category`, `month` are not required for this task.)

Typical conditions  

• `WHERE year = 2008` – to isolate 2008 data when determining the top‑5.  
• `WHERE year BETWEEN 2008 AND 2016` (or simply GROUP BY year) – to get annual numbers for all years held in the table.  

